# What Vercel does NOT need in the upload.
#
# Two traps are baked into this file's history, both worth keeping in mind:
#
#  1. services/, tests/ and blockchain/l3 are pnpm workspace members. Excluding them breaks
#     `pnpm install` at the root, because the lockfile expects their package.json to exist.
#     They stay — they are source only, and small.
#
#  2. A bare `docs` pattern matches at every depth, so it excluded apps/docs as well as the
#     top-level docs/. The build then failed with "No package found with name
#     '@kaurax/app-docs' in workspace", which points nowhere near the actual cause.
#     Anything meant to be root-only is anchored with a leading slash.
#
# docs/ itself is NOT excluded: apps/docs renders the repository's own documentation rather
# than keeping a second copy of it.

/.git
/.github
/.devnet
/.turbo
/blockchain/contracts/lib
/blockchain/contracts/out
/blockchain/contracts/cache
/blockchain/contracts/broadcast

node_modules
.next
dist
*.log
*.tar.zst
coverage
